      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal|Guarded Write Journal]] page describes **an in-memory transaction mechanism for file writes**. Here are the key points:\n\n1. **Prior State Recording**: Before the guarded tool executor overwrites a file, it records the file\u0027s previous state in an in-memory write journal \u2014 either the previous content if the file existed, or a note that it didn\u0027t exist.\n\n2. **Rollback on Failure**: If the agent run fails (due to turn cap exceeded, unrecoverable error, or denied writes), the journal can roll back all recorded writes in reverse order, restoring previous content or deleting newly created files.\n\n3. **All-or-Nothing Semantics**: This provides transactional all-or-nothing semantics for file writes without requiring a database \u2014 the journal itself acts as the transaction log, held in process memory for the duration of one run.\n\n4. **Query Agent Note**: The page also notes that the Query agent doesn\u0027t actually use the journal\u0027s rollback path since it has no write tool, though the journal type exists in the shared runtime library.",
